  data:  # c25b
    kind: work_item  # c25b
    title: "taint_refine.py: pin function-parameter receiver types to suppress str.replace / platform.system FPs in verify-claims"  # c25b
    status: todo_hard  # c25b
    priority: 2  # c25b
    parent:  # c25b
    tags:  # c25b
    - taint_flow  # c25b
    - self_analysis  # c25b
    - dogfooding  # c25b
    isbefore: []  # c25b
    duplicate_of: []  # c25b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # c25b
    pr_ref:  # c25b
    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-16.** `hypergumbo verify-claims --claims docs/hypergumbo.claims.yaml` reports 7/18 claims violated; this item covers the short-name-collision false-positive subset.\n\n**False positives.**\n\n- `cmd_add_extras → replace` (14 flows). Actual callsite: `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/cli.py:2554` — `name.replace(\"-\", \" \").capitalize()` where `name` is a function parameter (str). Collides with `pathlib.Path.replace` (which IS a fs_write sink).\n- `cmd_install_gitleaks → system` (4 flows). Actual callsite: `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/gitleaks.py:114` — `platform.system().lower()`. Collides with `os.system` (which IS a subprocess sink). `os.system` is not used anywhere in gitleaks.py.\n\nAlso implicated: the `run = runner if runner is not None else subprocess.run` indirection at `rust_analyzer_install.py:111/140/202` — local variable rebinding hides the receiver type from `_sink_module_compatible`.\n\n**Root cause.** `taint_refine.py` rewrites unresolved-receiver dsts via import-rooted RHS chains and `from`-import aliases, but explicitly documents (module docstring lines 44-52) that these receiver classes are OUT of scope:\n\n1. Function-parameter receivers (`def f(name): name.replace(...)`) — the `replace` case\n2. Call-RHS bindings (`run = ... else subprocess.run; run(...)`) — the rust-analyzer case\n3. Closure captures\n4. Aliased module attributes (`platform.system()` — module name resolved, but short-name collision with `os.system` evades `_sink_module_compatible` because `platform` isn't in the sink module set)\n\n`_sink_module_compatible` at `taint.py:804-842` exempts `external` edges (per the WI-sikur design) to allow the post-DDG refinement pass to run, but this exemption also lets the FPs through when refinement can't pin the receiver.\n\n**Fix proposal.** Two complementary paths:\n\n1. **Parameter-receiver type pinning** in `taint_refine.py`. Walk function-signature annotations: when a parameter has a `str` / `bytes` / `Path` / `list` annotation, propagate that type to short-name call resolutions inside the function body. Smallest extension; closes the `str.replace` FP class.\n2. **Module-name conflict map** in `_sink_module_compatible`. When the candidate sink module is `os.system` but the resolved receiver carries module hint `platform`, reject the match even on the `external` exemption path. Requires extending the Python io_primitives YAML with explicit `mutually_exclusive_modules` or building it from the sink set.\n\n(1) is mechanical; (2) needs a small design note. Suggested ordering: (1) first, then evaluate (2) against any residual FPs.\n\n**Test fixture.** `packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/` should grow a fixture in `test_taint_refine.py` exercising `def f(name: str): name.replace(...)` and asserting the `Path.replace` sink does NOT match."  # c25b
    fields: {}  # c25b
